Here is the plain C kernel:
```cpp
#include "correlation.h"


void kernel_correlation( 
			double float_n,
			double data[ N + 0][M + 0],
			double corr[ M + 0][M + 0],
			double mean[ M + 0],
			double stddev[ M + 0])
{


    const int n = N;
    const int m = M;

  int i, j, k;

  double eps = 0.1;


  for (j = 0; j < m; j++)
    {
      mean[j] = 0.0;
      for (i = 0; i < n; i++)
	mean[j] += data[i][j];
      mean[j] /= float_n;
    }


   for (j = 0; j < m; j++)
    {
      stddev[j] = 0.0;
      for (i = 0; i < n; i++)
        stddev[j] += (data[i][j] - mean[j]) * (data[i][j] - mean[j]);
      stddev[j] /= float_n;
      stddev[j] = sqrt(stddev[j]);


      stddev[j] = stddev[j] <= eps ? 1.0 : stddev[j];
    }


  for (i = 0; i < n; i++)
    for (j = 0; j < m; j++)
      {
        data[i][j] -= mean[j];
        data[i][j] /= sqrt(float_n) * stddev[j];
      }


  for (i = 0; i < m-1; i++)
    {
      corr[i][i] = 1.0;
      for (j = i+1; j < m; j++)
        {
          corr[i][j] = 0.0;
          for (k = 0; k < n; k++)
            corr[i][j] += (data[k][i] * data[k][j]);
          corr[j][i] = corr[i][j];
        }
    }
  corr[m-1][m-1] = 1.0;

}
```

Provide the complete HLS-optimized code in a ```cpp code fence.

## Optimization skills you may reference (curated, benchmark-neutral)

Apply only the skills whose `When applicable` matches the current state. Treat `Guards` as hard constraints. Avoid-rules (kind=avoid_rule) describe things NOT to do.

### prompt-tiling
(kind=compound_transformation, confidence=medium)
When applicable: a loop nest repeatedly accesses a bounded region of a large array, matrix, grid, or neighbor window from global memory, and this region can be staged locally to enable reuse, pipelining, unrolling, or local-buffer partitioning
Strategy: do not tile only because the array is large; reshape the loop nest around tiles, stage the reusable working set into local memory, rewrite compute indexing to use local tile coordinates, and exploit the local tile through pipelining, inner-loop unrolling, and buffer partitioning when legal
Guards:
  - do not tile only because an array is large
  - do not apply tiling if each element is streamed once with no reuse or scheduling benefit
  - do not simply copy data into a local buffer while leaving scalar compute unchanged
  - do not allocate dynamic or excessively large tile buffers
  - preserve boundary conditions and numerical behavior

### prompt-pipeline
(kind=compound_transformation, confidence=high)
When applicable: a frequently executed loop is scheduled sequentially or has high interval, and the loop body is pipeline-eligible after resolving true dependencies, memory-port limits, global-memory access issues, or serialized inner-loop body latency
Strategy: do not only insert a PIPELINE pragma; choose the right hot loop, request a realistic II, and restructure dependencies, memory accesses, local buffers, and small inner loops so the achieved II actually improves
Guards:
  - do not add PIPELINE blindly without checking achieved II
  - do not use dependence inter false on a real loop-carried dependence
  - do not pipeline an outer loop if it causes unintended full unrolling or resource explosion
  - do not ignore memory-port conflicts after pipelining
  - do not claim success if the report still shows the same II bottleneck

### prompt-unroll
(kind=compound_transformation, confidence=high)
When applicable: a loop has independent iterations or a safely transformable reduction, and latency is dominated by arithmetic throughput rather than global-memory bandwidth
Strategy: apply partial or complete unrolling only after confirming independence or safe reduction structure; match array partitioning/banking to the unroll factor and verify resource growth
Guards:
  - do not unroll memory-bound loops before fixing bandwidth or locality
  - do not unroll across true loop-carried dependencies
  - for floating-point reductions, confirm tolerance permits reassociation
  - do not complete-partition large arrays blindly

### prompt-doublebuffer
(kind=compound_transformation, confidence=high)
When applicable: load, compute, and/or store phases operate on consecutive chunks or tiles but currently execute serially with no overlap
Strategy: create ping-pong local buffers and a legal producer/consumer schedule so load of tile k+1 overlaps compute of tile k and optionally store of tile k-1
Guards:
  - do not add two buffers if phases still execute serially
  - do not use DATAFLOW when stage dependencies prevent overlap
  - avoid double buffering if local memory usage becomes excessive
  - preserve first-tile and last-tile behavior

```cpp
#include "correlation.h"

extern "C" {

void kernel_correlation(
            double float_n,
            double data[ N + 0][M + 0],
            double corr[ M + 0][M + 0],
            double mean[ M + 0],
            double stddev[ M + 0])
{
#pragma HLS INTERFACE m_axi port=data   offset=slave bundle=gmem
#pragma HLS INTERFACE m_axi port=corr   offset=slave bundle=gmem
#pragma HLS INTERFACE m_axi port=mean   offset=slave bundle=gmem
#pragma HLS INTERFACE m_axi port=stddev offset=slave bundle=gmem
#pragma HLS INTERFACE s_axilite port=float_n bundle=control
#pragma HLS INTERFACE s_axilite port=data    bundle=control
#pragma HLS INTERFACE s_axilite port=corr    bundle=control
#pragma HLS INTERFACE s_axilite port=mean    bundle=control
#pragma HLS INTERFACE s_axilite port=stddev  bundle=control
#pragma HLS INTERFACE s_axilite port=return  bundle=control

    // Local copies for fully parallel access
    double l_data   [N][M];
    double l_corr   [M][M];
    double l_mean   [M];
    double l_stddev [M];

#pragma HLS ARRAY_PARTITION variable=l_data    cyclic factor=8 dim=2
#pragma HLS ARRAY_PARTITION variable=l_corr    cyclic factor=8 dim=2
#pragma HLS ARRAY_PARTITION variable=l_mean    complete dim=1
#pragma HLS ARRAY_PARTITION variable=l_stddev  complete dim=1

    // -------------------------------------------------------
    // Load data from global memory
    // -------------------------------------------------------
    load_data_i: for (int i = 0; i < N; i++) {
        load_data_j: for (int j = 0; j < M; j++) {
#pragma HLS PIPELINE II=1
            l_data[i][j] = data[i][j];
        }
    }

    const int n = N;
    const int m = M;
    double eps = 0.1;

    // -------------------------------------------------------
    // Compute mean
    // -------------------------------------------------------
    mean_j: for (int j = 0; j < m; j++) {
        double sum = 0.0;
        mean_i: for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
#pragma HLS PIPELINE II=1
            sum += l_data[i][j];
        }
        l_mean[j] = sum / float_n;
    }

    // -------------------------------------------------------
    // Compute stddev
    // -------------------------------------------------------
    stddev_j: for (int j = 0; j < m; j++) {
        double sum = 0.0;
        stddev_i: for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
#pragma HLS PIPELINE II=1
            double diff = l_data[i][j] - l_mean[j];
            sum += diff * diff;
        }
        double s = sum / float_n;
        s = sqrt(s);
        l_stddev[j] = (s <= eps) ? 1.0 : s;
    }

    // -------------------------------------------------------
    // Center and normalize data
    // -------------------------------------------------------
    double sqrt_float_n = sqrt(float_n);
    norm_i: for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
        norm_j: for (int j = 0; j < m; j++) {
#pragma HLS PIPELINE II=1
            l_data[i][j] -= l_mean[j];
            l_data[i][j] /= sqrt_float_n * l_stddev[j];
        }
    }

    // -------------------------------------------------------
    // Compute correlation matrix
    // -------------------------------------------------------
    corr_i: for (int i = 0; i < m - 1; i++) {
        l_corr[i][i] = 1.0;
        corr_j: for (int j = i + 1; j < m; j++) {
            double sum = 0.0;
            corr_k: for (int k = 0; k < n; k++) {
#pragma HLS PIPELINE II=1
                sum += l_data[k][i] * l_data[k][j];
            }
            l_corr[i][j] = sum;
            l_corr[j][i] = sum;
        }
    }
    l_corr[m-1][m-1] = 1.0;

    // -------------------------------------------------------
    // Store results to global memory
    // -------------------------------------------------------
    store_mean_j: for (int j = 0; j < m; j++) {
#pragma HLS PIPELINE II=1
        mean[j]   = l_mean[j];
        stddev[j] = l_stddev[j];
    }

    store_corr_i: for (int i = 0; i < m; i++) {
        store_corr_j: for (int j = 0; j < m; j++) {
#pragma HLS PIPELINE II=1
            corr[i][j] = l_corr[i][j];
        }
    }

    store_data_i: for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
        store_data_j: for (int j = 0; j < m; j++) {
#pragma HLS PIPELINE II=1
            data[i][j] = l_data[i][j];
        }
    }
}

} // extern "C"
```

Looking at the current code, it already has local buffers (`l_data`, `l_corr`, `l_mean`, `l_stddev`) but loads/stores the entire arrays at once. The tiling optimization should restructure the code to process data in tiles/chunks, enabling better memory access patterns and locality.

For this correlation kernel, the key tiling opportunity is in the data loading and normalization phases - we can tile along the column (M) dimension when loading rows of data, and tile the correlation computation to work on column tiles.

```cpp
#include "correlation.h"
#include <cmath>

// Tile sizes
#define TILE_J 16   // tile size along M (column) dimension
#define TILE_I 16   // tile size along N (row) dimension

extern "C" {

// -------------------------------------------------------
// Load a tile of data: rows [i0, i0+TILE_I), cols [j0, j0+TILE_J)
// -------------------------------------------------------
static void load_data_tile(
    double data[N][M],
    double buf[TILE_I][TILE_J],
    int i0, int j0,
    int n, int m)
{
    for (int i = 0; i < TILE_I; i++) {
        for (int j = 0; j < TILE_J; j++) {
#pragma HLS PIPELINE II=1
            int gi = i0 + i;
            int gj = j0 + j;
            if (gi < n && gj < m)
                buf[i][j] = data[gi][gj];
            else
                buf[i][j] = 0.0;
        }
    }
}

// -------------------------------------------------------
// Store a tile of data back: rows [i0, i0+TILE_I), cols [j0, j0+TILE_J)
// -------------------------------------------------------
static void store_data_tile(
    double data[N][M],
    double buf[TILE_I][TILE_J],
    int i0, int j0,
    int n, int m)
{
    for (int i = 0; i < TILE_I; i++) {
        for (int j = 0; j < TILE_J; j++) {
#pragma HLS PIPELINE II=1
            int gi = i0 + i;
            int gj = j0 + j;
            if (gi < n && gj < m)
                data[gi][gj] = buf[i][j];
        }
    }
}

void kernel_correlation(
            double float_n,
            double data[ N + 0][M + 0],
            double corr[ M + 0][M + 0],
            double mean[ M + 0],
            double stddev[ M + 0])
{
#pragma HLS INTERFACE m_axi port=data   offset=slave bundle=gmem
#pragma HLS INTERFACE m_axi port=corr   offset=slave bundle=gmem
#pragma HLS INTERFACE m_axi port=mean   offset=slave bundle=gmem
#pragma HLS INTERFACE m_axi port=stddev offset=slave bundle=gmem
#pragma HLS INTERFACE s_axilite port=float_n bundle=control
#pragma HLS INTERFACE s_axilite port=data    bundle=control
#pragma HLS INTERFACE s_axilite port=corr    bundle=control
#pragma HLS INTERFACE s_axilite port=mean    bundle=control
#pragma HLS INTERFACE s_axilite port=stddev  bundle=control
#pragma HLS INTERFACE s_axilite port=return  bundle=control

    // -------------------------------------------------------
    // Full local arrays for intermediate computation
    // -------------------------------------------------------
    double l_data   [N][M];
    double l_corr   [M][M];
    double l_mean   [M];
    double l_stddev [M];

#pragma HLS ARRAY_PARTITION variable=l_data    cyclic factor=8 dim=2
#pragma HLS ARRAY_PARTITION variable=l_corr    cyclic factor=8 dim=2
#pragma HLS ARRAY_PARTITION variable=l_mean    complete dim=1
#pragma HLS ARRAY_PARTITION variable=l_stddev  complete dim=1

    // Tile buffer for load/store phases
    double tile_buf[TILE_I][TILE_J];
#pragma HLS ARRAY_PARTITION variable=tile_buf complete dim=2

    const int n = N;
    const int m = M;
    double eps = 0.1;

    // -------------------------------------------------------
    // LOAD PHASE: Load data from global memory in tiles
    // Tile along both N (rows) and M (cols) dimensions
    // -------------------------------------------------------
    load_tile_i: for (int i0 = 0; i0 < n; i0 += TILE_I) {
        load_tile_j: for (int j0 = 0; j0 < m; j0 += TILE_J) {
            // Load one tile from global memory into tile_buf
            load_gmem_i: for (int ti = 0; ti < TILE_I; ti++) {
                load_gmem_j: for (int tj = 0; tj < TILE_J; tj++) {
#pragma HLS PIPELINE II=1
                    int gi = i0 + ti;
                    int gj = j0 + tj;
                    if (gi < n && gj < m)
                        tile_buf[ti][tj] = data[gi][gj];
                    else
                        tile_buf[ti][tj] = 0.0;
                }
            }
            // Copy tile_buf into l_data
            copy_tile_i: for (int ti = 0; ti < TILE_I; ti++) {
                copy_tile_j: for (int tj = 0; tj < TILE_J; tj++) {
#pragma HLS PIPELINE II=1
                    int gi = i0 + ti;
                    int gj = j0 + tj;
                    if (gi < n && gj < m)
                        l_data[gi][gj] = tile_buf[ti][tj];
                }
            }
        }
    }

    // -------------------------------------------------------
    // COMPUTE PHASE 1: Compute mean (tiled over columns)
    // -------------------------------------------------------
    // Process columns in tiles of TILE_J
    mean_tile_j: for (int j0 = 0; j0 < m; j0 += TILE_J) {
        // For each column in this tile, accumulate sum over all rows
        // Use a local accumulator array for the tile columns
        double tile_sum[TILE_J];
#pragma HLS ARRAY_PARTITION variable=tile_sum complete dim=1

        // Initialize accumulators
        init_mean: for (int tj = 0; tj < TILE_J; tj++) {
#pragma HLS UNROLL
            tile_sum[tj] = 0.0;
        }

        // Accumulate over rows, processing TILE_J columns at a time
        mean_tile_i: for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
            mean_tile_jj: for (int tj = 0; tj < TILE_J; tj++) {
#pragma HLS PIPELINE II=1
                int gj = j0 + tj;
                if (gj < m)
                    tile_sum[tj] += l_data[i][gj];
            }
        }

        // Store means for this column tile
        store_mean_tile: for (int tj = 0; tj < TILE_J; tj++) {
#pragma HLS PIPELINE II=1
            int gj = j0 + tj;
            if (gj < m)
                l_mean[gj] = tile_sum[tj] / float_n;
        }
    }

    // -------------------------------------------------------
    // COMPUTE PHASE 2: Compute stddev (tiled over columns)
    // -------------------------------------------------------
    stddev_tile_j: for (int j0 = 0; j0 < m; j0 += TILE_J) {
        double tile_sum[TILE_J];
#pragma HLS ARRAY_PARTITION variable=tile_sum complete dim=1

        // Initialize
        init_stddev: for (int tj = 0; tj < TILE_J; tj++) {
#pragma HLS UNROLL
            tile_sum[tj] = 0.0;
        }

        // Accumulate squared differences
        stddev_tile_i: for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
            stddev_tile_jj: for (int tj = 0; tj < TILE_J; tj++) {
#pragma HLS PIPELINE II=1
                int gj = j0 + tj;
                if (gj < m) {
                    double diff = l_data[i][gj] - l_mean[gj];
                    tile_sum[tj] += diff * diff;
                }
            }
        }

        // Compute and store stddev for this column tile
        store_stddev_tile: for (int tj = 0; tj < TILE_J; tj++) {
#pragma HLS PIPELINE II=1
            int gj = j0 + tj;
            if (gj < m) {
                double s = tile_sum[tj] / float_n;
                s = sqrt(s);
                l_stddev[gj] = (s <= eps) ? 1.0 : s;
            }
        }
    }

    // -------------------------------------------------------
    // COMPUTE PHASE 3: Normalize data (tiled over rows x cols)
    // -------------------------------------------------------
    double sqrt_float_n = sqrt(float_n);

    norm_tile_i: for (int i0 = 0; i0 < n; i0 += TILE_I) {
        norm_tile_j: for (int j0 = 0; j0 < m; j0 += TILE_J) {
            // Load tile into tile_buf
            norm_load_i: for (int ti = 0; ti < TILE_I; ti++) {
                norm_load_j: for (int tj = 0; tj < TILE_J; tj++) {
#pragma HLS PIPELINE II=1
                    int gi = i0 + ti;
                    int gj = j0 + tj;
                    if (gi < n && gj < m)
                        tile_buf[ti][tj] = l_data[gi][gj];
                    else
                        tile_buf[ti][tj] = 0.0;
                }
            }

            // Normalize within tile
            norm_compute_i: for (int ti = 0; ti < TILE_I; ti++) {
                norm_compute_j: for (int tj = 0; tj < TILE_J; tj++) {
#pragma HLS PIPELINE II=1
                    int gi = i0 + ti;
                    int gj = j0 + tj;
                    if (gi < n && gj < m)
                        tile_buf[ti][tj] = tile_buf[ti][tj] / (sqrt_float_n * l_stddev[gj]);
                }
            }

            // Write normalized tile back to l_data
            norm_store_i: for (int ti = 0; ti < TILE_I; ti++) {
                norm_store_j: for (int tj = 0; tj < TILE_J; tj++) {
#pragma HLS PIPELINE II=1
                    int gi = i0 + ti;
                    int gj = j0 + tj;
                    if (gi < n && gj < m)
                        l_data[gi][gj] = tile_buf[ti][tj];
                }
            }
        }
    }

    // -------------------------------------------------------
    // COMPUTE PHASE 4: Correlation matrix (tiled over i,j pairs)
    // Tile over the output correlation matrix columns
    // -------------------------------------------------------
    corr_tile_i: for (int i = 0; i < m - 1; i++) {
        l_corr[i][i] = 1.0;

        // Tile j loop in chunks of TILE_J
        corr_tile_j: for (int j0 = i + 1; j0 < m; j0 += TILE_J) {
            // Accumulator for each j in the tile
            double tile_acc[TILE_J];
#pragma HLS ARRAY_PARTITION variable=tile_acc complete dim=1

            // Initialize accumulators
            init_corr: for (int tj = 0; tj < TILE_J; tj++) {
#pragma HLS UNROLL
                tile_acc[tj] = 0.0;
            }

            // Accumulate over rows k
            corr_k: for (int k = 0; k < n; k++) {
                double dki = l_data[k][i];
                corr_jj: for (int tj = 0; tj < TILE_J; tj++) {
#pragma HLS PIPELINE II=1
                    int gj = j0 + tj;
                    if (gj < m)
                        tile_acc[tj] += dki * l_data[k][gj];
                }
            }

            // Store tile results
            store_corr_tile: for (int tj = 0; tj < TILE_J; tj++) {
#pragma HLS PIPELINE II=1
                int gj = j0 + tj;
                if (gj < m) {
                    l_corr[i][gj] = tile_acc[tj];
                    l_corr[gj][i] = tile_acc[tj];
                }
            }
        }
    }
    l_corr[m-1][m-1] = 1.0;

    // -------------------------------------------------------
    // STORE PHASE: Write results back to global memory
    // -------------------------------------------------------

    // Store mean and stddev
    store_mean_j: for (int j = 0; j < m; j++) {
#pragma HLS PIPELINE II=1
        mean[j]   = l_mean[j];
        stddev[j] = l_stddev[j];
    }

    // Store correlation matrix in tiles
    store_corr_tile_i: for (int i0 = 0; i0 < m; i0 += TILE_J) {
        store_corr_tile_j: for (int j0 = 0; j0 < m; j0 += TILE_J) {
            // Load corr tile into tile_buf (reuse, note TILE_J x TILE_J)
            sc_load_i: for (int ti = 0; ti < TILE_J; ti++) {
                sc_load_j: for (int tj = 0; tj < TILE_J; tj++) {
#pragma HLS PIPELINE II=1
                    int gi = i0 + ti;
                    int gj = j0 + tj;
                    if (gi < m && gj < m)
                        tile_buf[ti][tj] = l_corr[gi][gj];
                    else
                        tile_buf[ti][tj] = 0.0;
                }
            }
            // Write tile to global memory
            sc_store_i: for (int ti = 0; ti < TILE_J; ti++) {
                sc_store_j: for (int tj = 0; tj < TILE_J; tj++) {
#pragma HLS PIPELINE II=1
                    int gi = i0 + ti;
                    int gj = j0 + tj;
                    if (gi < m && gj < m)
                        corr[gi][gj] = tile_buf[ti][tj];
                }
            }
        }
    }

    // Store normalized data in tiles
    store_data_tile_i: for (int i0 = 0; i0 < n; i0 += TILE_I) {
        store_data_tile_j: for (int j0 = 0; j0 < m; j0 += TILE_J) {
            // Load l_data tile into tile_buf
            sd_load_i: for (int ti = 0; ti < TILE_I; ti++) {
                sd_load_j: for (int tj = 0; tj < TILE_J; tj++) {
#pragma HLS PIPELINE II=1
                    int gi = i0 + ti;
                    int gj = j0 + tj;
                    if (gi < n && gj < m)
                        tile_buf[ti][tj] = l_data[gi][gj];
                    else
                        tile_buf[ti][tj] = 0.0;
                }
            }
            // Write tile to global memory
            sd_store_i: for (int ti = 0; ti < TILE_I; ti++) {
                sd_store_j: for (int tj = 0; tj < TILE_J; tj++) {
#pragma HLS PIPELINE II=1
                    int gi = i0 + ti;
                    int gj = j0 + tj;
                    if (gi < n && gj < m)
                        data[gi][gj] = tile_buf[ti][tj];
                }
            }
        }
    }
