Looking at the current code, I need to apply double buffering to overlap the load phase with the compute/store phases. The main opportunity is in the initial data load phase (loading from global memory into `l_data`) and the final store phases. I'll create ping-pong tile buffers so that while one tile is being loaded from global memory, the previous tile can be copied into `l_data`.

The key double-buffering opportunity is in the load loop nest and the store loop nests, where we alternate between two tile buffers.

